# The Zenbook A16's WSA884x speaker amplifiers often come back from a SoundWire
# clock stop unattached, or with every register reading 0x21, so a bus's
# speakers fall silent until the next stop. Keep both WSA SoundWire controllers out of runtime
# suspend so the bus never stops its clock. It costs well under 0.1 W.
ACTION=="add|bind", SUBSYSTEM=="platform", ENV{OF_COMPATIBLE_0}=="qcom,soundwire-v3.1.0", \
  KERNEL=="6c80000.soundwire|6ca0000.soundwire", \
  ATTR{[dmi/id]board_name}=="UX3607OA", ATTR{power/control}="on"
